WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:02.589
- To celebrate our season
three premiere this week,

00:00:02.589 --> 00:00:04.931
we've been asking some
friends of the show,

00:00:04.931 --> 00:00:09.199
here in LA, to share
their LA top three lists.

00:00:09.199 --> 00:00:12.866
♪LA top 3♪

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.471
These are the off-the-beaten-path,
personalized picks

00:00:17.471 --> 00:00:20.219
from people who have
lived in LA for years.

00:00:20.219 --> 00:00:22.930
Today's top three comes from
one of our favorite guests

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:24.700
at the show, one of my favorites.

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:26.580
Let's head out to the literal field

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:27.620
where traffic anchor,

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:29.640
Robin Winston from our partner station,

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:32.727
NBC for Los Angeles has more
on this developing story.

00:00:32.727 --> 00:00:33.743
(audience clapping)

00:00:33.743 --> 00:00:36.586
- Hi, Kelly. It's so nice
to see you. And by the way,

00:00:36.586 --> 00:00:38.820
I hope you had a decent
commute heading to work

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:39.653
this morning.

00:00:39.653 --> 00:00:40.910
I know the LA traffic can be a little bit

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:41.838
of a headache sometimes,

00:00:41.838 --> 00:00:45.050
but we're out here in some
little known bucolic pastors,

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:46.140
just outside of Los Angeles,

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:48.540
where it's absolutely beautiful.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:50.740
It's so peaceful. It's so chill here.

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:51.573
Trust me,

00:00:51.573 --> 00:00:52.770
when you get here, you're
not going to have to worry

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:54.380
about bumper to bumper traffic.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:56.190
- And it looks like you're
at a ranch or something.

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:57.670
I want to go where you're at right now.

00:00:57.670 --> 00:01:00.804
So will you introduce us to
the Secret Celebrity Selector

00:01:00.804 --> 00:01:03.310
of today's LA top three lists?

00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:05.010
- Absolutely. I'll give you a little hint.

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:06.772
She's one of the nicest
people in Hollywood,

00:01:06.772 --> 00:01:07.949
I can vouch for that,

00:01:07.949 --> 00:01:10.670
and you'll know her from
How I Met Your Mother.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:12.191
It's Alyson Hannigan.

00:01:12.191 --> 00:01:13.524
(audience cheering)

00:01:13.524 --> 00:01:15.159
- Hi Kelly.

00:01:15.159 --> 00:01:19.410
- Hi. (clapping) I wanna
be where you are right now.

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:20.243
It looks awesome.

00:01:20.243 --> 00:01:22.040
- You definitely want to be where I am.

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:23.607
- I do. How's your family?

00:01:23.607 --> 00:01:25.071
- Good, how's yours?

00:01:25.071 --> 00:01:26.440
- Oh, they're so good.

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:28.620
I'm so glad they're in
school. Amen. God bless.

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:31.111
Please keep them all in school. (laughs)

00:01:31.111 --> 00:01:34.274
So Alison, you're giving
us your top three places to

00:01:34.274 --> 00:01:37.010
entertain your kids in Los Angeles,

00:01:37.010 --> 00:01:39.360
while you're really
tricking them into learning.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:41.276
So what's number three?

00:01:41.276 --> 00:01:44.350
- Okay. So number three
would be Underwood Farms,

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:45.650
which is like a big...

00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:48.367
you can pick... a farm where
you can pick your own fruits or

00:01:48.367 --> 00:01:50.657
vegetables or pumpkins around Halloween.

00:01:50.657 --> 00:01:55.000
I really love that because it
just really teaches your kids

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:59.948
how the stuff that they have
in their lunchbox is grown.

00:01:59.948 --> 00:02:03.940
So that's number three. Number
two would be Bob Baker's,

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:05.330
Marionette Puppet Theater,

00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:07.700
which is such a wonderful experience,

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:10.110
especially for little
ones. And I'm so crafty.

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:12.489
I just really just
enjoyed the art department

00:02:12.489 --> 00:02:14.620
and how they make these puppets.

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:18.729
And you learn so much about
all the history of puppetry.

00:02:18.729 --> 00:02:20.507
And it's just wonderful.

00:02:20.507 --> 00:02:24.472
But the number one is, where I am today,

00:02:24.472 --> 00:02:27.400
The Gentle Barn,

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:30.530
where you can come and hug cows,

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:34.300
all of these beautiful, wonderful animals

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:39.975
have been rescued and
they're so well loved

00:02:39.975 --> 00:02:43.644
and taken care of, and
you can just hug them.

00:02:43.644 --> 00:02:45.973
And they're so lovely.

00:02:47.516 --> 00:02:50.020
And then you'll just never want to leave.

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:52.390
- I love all your places.
Those were such great ones.

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:53.223
Thank you so much.

00:02:53.223 --> 00:02:54.056
(audience clapping)

00:02:54.056 --> 00:02:55.650
It's always good to see you Alyson.

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:57.780
And you too, Robin.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:01.018
Y'all have fun for me. I want to be there.

00:03:01.018 --> 00:03:02.340
(audience cheering)

